        "original_id": "95369608-3777-5b30-9fd3-a805ffabbc81",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gustave-Hippolyte Roger, Hector Berlioz, Giacomo Meyerbeer, Daniel Auber\n- Works: La damnation de Faust, Le prophète, L'enfant prodigue\n- Places: Opéra-Comique, Paris\n- Roles: leading tenor roles, Azaël\n\nFacts:\n- Gustave-Hippolyte Roger was the celebrated French tenor who sang the role of Azaël in the premiere of Daniel Auber's L'enfant prodigue.\n- On 6 December 1846, Hector Berlioz's La damnation de Faust was first performed at the Opéra-Comique in Paris.\n- In 1846, Gustave-Hippolyte Roger created the leading tenor role in Hector Berlioz's La damnation de Faust.\n- In 1849, Gustave-Hippolyte Roger created the leading tenor role in Giacomo Meyerbeer's Le prophète.\n- Gustave-Hippolyte Roger is best known for creating the leading tenor roles in La damnation de Faust and Le prophète.",
